From: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: restore factory RX limits after tc teardown

The AN7581 QDMA initialization now installs the factory RX ring limits,
including the control-ring rates on rings 6, 7, 8 and 11. The tc matchall
destroy path still programs rate zero for every allocated RX ring, which
removes those defaults after a police filter is deleted.

Restore the complete AN7581 factory table when the police filter is torn
down. Preserve the existing disable behavior on other SoCs.

Signed-off-by: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4119,9 +4119,12 @@ static int airoha_dev_tc_matchall(struct net_device *netdev,
 			rate = rate << 3; /* Kbps */
 			bucket_size = act->police.burst;
 		}
-		fallthrough;
+		return airoha_qdma_set_rx_meter(dev, rate, bucket_size,
+						unit_type);
 	}
 	case TC_CLSMATCHALL_DESTROY:
+		if (airoha_is_7581(dev->eth))
+			return airoha_qdma_set_factory_rx_limits(airoha_qdma_deref(dev));
 		return airoha_qdma_set_rx_meter(dev, rate, bucket_size,
 						unit_type);
 	default:
